  offerDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - That road leads out of <b><#E09500>Canyon Crossing</color></b>.
    - The <b><#E09500>Town River</color></b> is beyond it.
    - "There\u2019s already another way there, but this would give the region a much
      more direct connection."
    - "Finish this crossing, and the route you\u2019ve built will finally lead beyond
      the canyon."
    - This crossing will carry a heavier vehicle than the ones before it.
    - This time, pay attention to more than just where the vehicle is.
    - <b><#E09500>Watch how the rest of the structure responds as the load moves
      across</color></b>.
    - <b><#E09500>Keep an eye on how the different parts behave during the test</color></b>.
    - "If you\u2019re ready, take the contract.\r\n"
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - "Don\u2019t focus on just one part of the bridge."
    - 'Watch how the whole structure responds as the vehicle moves across. '
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences: []
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - "That\u2019s it."
    - The eastern passage is open.
    - 'You started by connecting Central Canyonville to the factory.

'
    - Then you improved the route through the canyon and brought it all the way to
      the community.
    - Now that route leads toward the <b><#E09500>Town River</color></b>.
